[h2]Build 0.9.139[/h2]
[h3]Changed[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Any gear can now be recycled[/b], at the benches and the industrial repair center. What it gives back comes from what the item says it is made of, then from the recipe that makes it; if neither says, it is still recycled but gives nothing back. No more "cannot be recycled".
[*]Gear nothing says the materials of (no cost and no recipe - quest rewards, relics, trader-only gear) is no longer repaired for free: it costs a plain material worth about half the item's value for a full rebuild - cloth for apparel, steel for weapons, plasteel for spacer-tech gear and better - scaled by damage like any repair.
[/list]
[h3]Added[/h3]
[list]
[*][b]Material filters:[/b] item filters (bench bills, the repair center's bills, stockpiles) get "allow made of cloth", "allow made of leather", "allow made of metal" and "allow made of wood" under Apparel, and metal and wood under Weapons. Untick one to leave out gear made of that. "Made of" is the item's material, or the main material in its build cost - a steel flak vest counts as metal.
[/list]
